#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""stile — inverse printf whose proving string must be distinctive.

weld (mutation-59) welds concat backward from a later string. A 4-char
suffix (`{body}abcd`) and a fence closer leftover (`\\n```) were still
templates. stile: a proving string that is only a newline / fence marker /
<4 distinctive static chars is not a template unless there are ≥2
expression holes. Incomplete fence leftovers refuse (caulk complete
operand). `response() + "\\nDone."` still binds. Middle-drop still a miss.

Stream filter. No walk. No second inverse-printf walker.
"""

